From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenSec <contactus@opensec.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:06:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] macOS: SharedArrayBuffer with the JIT off

With the JIT off and the mach exception handler sandbox policy unknown, JSC on Darwin takes the process for sandboxed and turns
SharedArrayBuffer (and Wasm's fast memory) off: an ahead-of-time executable built with the JIT off had no SharedArrayBuffer,
which Pi's codemode worker needs. Bun is not sandboxed; it now says so before JSC is initialized.
---
 src/jsc/bindings/ZigGlobalObject.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/jsc/bindings/ZigGlobalObject.cpp b/src/jsc/bindings/ZigGlobalObject.cpp
index f8b692c4..bb219910 100644
--- a/src/jsc/bindings/ZigGlobalObject.cpp
+++ b/src/jsc/bindings/ZigGlobalObject.cpp
@@ -304,6 +304,12 @@ extern "C" void JSCInitialize(const char* envp[], size_t envc, void (*onCrash)(c
         // Before any option is set: with the AOT engine, Options::notifyOptionsChanged() turns useJIT off for good if the compilers
         // are not installed (CompilerHooks.h). This also installs the compiler of images for `bun build --compile`.
         JSC::installCompilers();
+#if OS(DARWIN)
+        // Bun is no sandboxed process: mach exception handlers are allowed. Unknown, JSC takes a JIT turned off (as in an
+        // ahead-of-time executable) for a sign of a sandbox that blocks them, and turns SharedArrayBuffer and Wasm's fast
+        // memory off with it.
+        JSC::Options::machExceptionHandlerSandboxPolicy = JSC::Options::SandboxPolicy::Allow;
+#endif
         Bun__ensureICUDefaultLocale();
         JSC::Config::enableRestrictedOptions();
         // JSC options come from BUN_JSC_* (applied in the callback below), not JSC_*.
